1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1  "Software" means the Protein Studio application and its source code as
     distributed by the Licensor, including the Python package under
     src/protein_studio/, the test suite, the example data, the build and
     documentation tooling, and any documentation shipped with it.

1.2  "Licensor" means Zhengwei Xie (谢正伟), the copyright holder of the
     Software, or any successor entity he designates in writing.

1.3  "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising the permissions
     granted by this License.

1.4  "Academic Use" means use for scientific research, education, scholarly
     communication, or other not-for-profit scholarly activity, in each case
     without seeking or deriving commercial advantage from the Software
     itself.

1.5  "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software — in original or modified
     form, in source or binary form, alone or combined with other software —
     that is undertaken for, or in the course of, a commercial activity or
     business. Commercial Use includes, without limitation: embedding the
     Software in a product or service offered for money or to a paying
     customer; using it as part of a paid service, a contract research
     engagement, or a consultancy deliverable; using it to make decisions
     whose primary purpose is commercial gain; and distributing the Software
     as part of a commercially offered offering.

1.6  "Output" means any image, rendering, measurement, structure, trajectory
     annotation, distance, score, or other result produced by running the
     Software.

1.7  "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, or that incorporates
     code, structure, design, or other elements of, the Software.

1.8  "Third-Party Components" means the third-party libraries and other
     materials listed in Section 6.

